# Dhan access tokens live exactly 24 hours and no long-lived credential can
# replace them: the 12-month API key only MINTS a token, and minting needs an
# interactive browser login with 2FA. /v2/RenewToken is the only automatable
# path, and it only extends a token that is still ACTIVE.
#
# TIMED TO THE EC2 SCHEDULE, NOT TO THE CLOCK. The instance runs
# 08:15-23:55 IST Mon-Fri. Cron does not catch up runs missed while the box
# was off, so any slot outside that window silently never fires - the
# previous "every 6 hours" schedule had 00:00 UTC (05:30 IST) doing exactly
# that. Both entries below sit safely inside the uptime window.
#
# 16:30 UTC = 22:00 IST, ~2h before shutdown. Threshold 25 is deliberately
# above the 24h token life so this ALWAYS renews, sending a full-life token
# into the 8.3h overnight gap (13.75h still left at the next boot). Renewing
# early costs nothing - it just resets the 24h clock.
#
# 02:50 UTC = 08:20 IST, ~5 minutes after boot and ~40 minutes before the
# 09:00 NSE open. Safety net at the default 12h threshold, for the night the
# 22:00 run failed or the box came up late.
#
# WEEKENDS ARE NOT SOLVABLE HERE. Fri 23:55 -> Mon 08:15 is 56.3h against a
# 24h token, so Friday's token is expired before Monday and an expired token
# cannot be renewed, only regenerated by hand at web.dhan.co. Monday's 08:20
# run will therefore FAIL by design; it exists to say "MANUAL ACTION
# REQUIRED" in the log at 08:20 rather than let the 09:00 open arrive as a
# wall of 401s. Do not "fix" it by adding weekend entries - the box is off.
#
# Output goes to a log (no MTA on this host); the script exits non-zero and
# logs a FAILED line on every failure path, which is the alerting surface.
50 2 * * 1-5 root /opt/option-decode/ops/scripts/dhan-token-renew.sh >> /opt/option-decode-native/logs/dhan-token-renew.log 2>&1
30 16 * * 1-5 root /opt/option-decode/ops/scripts/dhan-token-renew.sh --threshold-hours 25 >> /opt/option-decode-native/logs/dhan-token-renew.log 2>&1
